    {
        "content": "<p>Wouldn't the idiomatic way be checking for <code>xs.size = 0</code>?</p>",
        "id": 597538217,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1779717398
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, there is no difference in speed actually (because of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Array.instDecidableEqEmpImpl#doc\">docs#Array.instDecidableEqEmpImpl</a>) and in certain situations, you need a <code>x ≠ #[]</code> hypothesis and not a <code>xs.size &gt; 0</code> hypothesis (take e.g. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Array.min#doc\">docs#Array.min</a>). In other situations, <code>xs.size &gt; 0</code> might be more convenient though.</p>",
        "id": 597539089,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1779717788
    }
